kind how-do-i
title How do I make a new look and use it on the console?
intro A look is a font set, a size and a color scheme that a terminal draws in. You make a look in the Looks tab, and give it to a terminal in the Flow tab.
see looks/try-a-whole-look-on-the-console
see install-and-restore/save-on-quit-and-install-from-the-command-line

# The machine: vtium runs one head, console, on VT 5, in the built-in
# font. The font set mono draws the bitmap font mono.bdf, which is
# installed and active.
file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
draft from-installed

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Choose New look.
3. Erase the name.
4. Type big.
5. Press Enter.
note The look's card opens. Its lines are the look's name, font set, size and color scheme.
6. Set Font set to mono.
7. Choose Size.
8. Choose 24 pt.
9. Set Color scheme to vga.
10. Press Esc.
at the look is made
check screen shows "big uses the font set"

11. Go to the Flow tab.
12. Choose console.
13. Set Look to big.
14. Press Esc.
at the look is on the console's terminal
check screen shows "look big"

15. Press s to save.
16. Press i to install.
note vtium-config asks before it installs the draft.
17. Press y.
at the install
check draft head console look big
check draft look big font-name mono
check installed head console font-name mono
check installed head console font-size 24
check installed head console palette vga

18. Press q to quit.
19. Restart vtium.
at the restart
check exited 0
check console draws mono
check console cell 16x32
check console palette vga
